{
"All four of these rulers owed their success to foreigners. Looking at it this way, how have foreigners failed Ch'in?": "1e0804d5d756",
"Beating jars and knocking on pots, plucking the cheng and slapping the thigh, singing out wu-wu to please the ear — that is the true music of Ch'in.": "6858781a4326",
"But in choosing men it is not so: no asking whether a man is able, no weighing of right and wrong; whoever is not of Ch'in must go, whoever is a foreigner is expelled.": "4e318b47da0e",
"But now you cast away the common people to enrich enemy states and turn back guests to build up the other lords, so that the able men of the world draw back and dare not face west, binding their feet and refusing to enter Ch'in.": "5f95c0b6ed57",
"Duke Hsiao used the laws of Shang Yang: customs were changed, the people grew prosperous, the state grew rich and strong, the common people served willingly and the other lords submitted; he took the armies of Ch'u and Wei and a thousand li of land, and to this day the state is well governed and strong.": "4c8f3f75137c",
"Had those four turned foreigners away and not admitted them, kept able men at a distance and not used them, the state would have had no real wealth and Ch'in no name for greatness.": "c965bbeff5b6",
"I have heard that where the land is broad the grain is plentiful, where the state is large the people are many, and where the arms are strong the soldiers are brave.": "dd89b1dfac44",
"I hear that the officials are deliberating on expelling foreigners. I venture to think this a mistake.": "227dbf6e5a9b",
"If a thing must be produced in Ch'in before it may be used, then the night-shining disc would not adorn the court, vessels of rhinoceros horn and ivory would not be objects of pleasure,": "629b35b25c04",
"If everything that adorns the inner palace, fills the lower ranks, pleases the mind and delights the ear and eye had to come from Ch'in,": "aa18bd33e670",
"If so, then what you value lies in women, music, pearls and jade, and what you make light of lies in people.": "b54f8e52116a",
"King Chao got Fan Chü: he dismissed the Marquis of Jang and drove out the Lord of Hua-yang, strengthened the royal house and shut out the private clans, ate away at the other lords like a silkworm, and brought Ch'in to imperial greatness.": "5ac9b46fa08d",
"King Hui used the schemes of Chang I: he seized the lands of the Three Rivers, annexed Pa and Shu in the west, took Shang commandery in the north and Han-chung in the south, enclosed the Nine Yi, subdued Yen and Ying, held the pass of Ch'eng-kao in the east, and carved off the richest soil;": "ca02cd92eff6",
"Long ago Duke Mu sought out able men: from the west he took Yu Yü from the Jung, from the east he got Pai-li Hsi from Wan, he welcomed Chien Shu from Sung, and sought out P'i Pao and Kung-sun Chih from Chin.": "73a068024faf",
"Many things not produced in Ch'in are worth treasuring; many men not born in Ch'in are willing to be loyal.": "17dc35a0f554",
"Now Your Majesty brings in jade from the K'un mountains, holds the treasures of Sui and Ho, hangs the bright-moon pearl, wears the T'ai-a sword, rides the Hsien-li horse, raises the kingfisher-phoenix banner, and sets up drums of sacred crocodile hide.": "1990f95afd63",
"Now to expel foreigners and so enrich enemy states, to reduce your own people and so add to your foes, to hollow yourself out within while planting resentment among the lords without — and then to seek that the state be free from danger: that cannot be had.": "528b815e0bba",
"Now you set aside the jar-beating and take up Cheng and Wei, put away the cheng and choose the Shao-yü. Why is that?": "79e9a5d856f8",
"Of these several treasures Ch'in produces not one, and yet Your Majesty delights in them. Why?": "e1c08426caf9",
"Simply because it pleases you here and now, and is agreeable to look upon.": "e277815f6bea",
"The songs of Cheng, Wei and Sang-chien, and the Shao-yü and the Wu-hsiang — these are the music of other states.": "bd4438409e2d",
"Therefore Mount T'ai does not refuse a clod of earth, and so achieves its greatness; the rivers and the sea do not pick among small streams, and so achieve their depth;": "a5aedfaa3eb0",
"These five men were not born in Ch'in, yet Duke Mu employed them; he annexed twenty states and became overlord of the western Jung.": "21536406aecf",
"This is not the way to bestride all within the seas and hold the other lords in check.": "43bf0b2ad691",
"This is what is called lending weapons to a bandit and handing provisions to a thief.": "f280d5028ca8",
"Thus the land has no four quarters and the people no foreign states; the four seasons are full and fair and the gods send down blessings. This is why the Five Emperors and the Three Kings had no equal.": "016c31323754",
"and a true king does not turn back the multitude, and so makes his virtue shine.": "85c57c7d4b49",
"so he broke up the north-south alliance of the six states and made them face west and serve Ch'in — and the benefit reaches to this day.": "2a608139977a",
"then pins set with Wan pearls, earrings hung with fine beads, robes of O silk and brocade ornaments would not be brought before you; and the graceful, elegant women of Chao would not stand at your side.": "b30a804f5465",
"women of Cheng and Wei would not fill the inner palace, fine horses would not fill the outer stables, the gold and tin of Chiang-nan would go unused, and the cinnabar and azurite of western Shu would not be taken for pigment.": "1de3745d5acf"
